WEBVTT

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.100
C'mon. Hurry and get in.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.000
Y-You don't understand...

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.030
I have to go to Mitsutomo
Corporation and...

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.880
Let me off!

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.940
To ditch an interview
with our company...

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:46.820
Is he that outstanding
of a student?

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.860
Damn that, Godai!
How dare he not show up! Damn!

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:59.050
Congratulations!
It's a healthy boy!

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:07.740
I'm sure the amulet
worked its charm.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.980
Yes. It was an easier birth
than expected.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.060
Want to stop for a drink?
I know of a good place nearby.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.510
It'd be useless to explain
why I'm so late.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.680
Mitsutomo Corporation...
what a short-lived dream.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:58.120
What?! He didn't show for
the interview? Why not?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.020
How should I know?
No matter what the reason

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:06.300
he's not ready for the real world
if he can shirk the interview.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.800
I'm sure there's a
good reason.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.590
Dad!

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.550
It's not like Godai to be
irresponsible like that.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.210
Please... do something.
Dad!

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.370
No matter what the excuse
it's too late!

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.610
I'll go talk to him.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.490
- Ibuki! It's dinner time!
- Let her go.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:36.740
Why, Godai?
What happened?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.330
What's wrong, you guys?

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.460
He's playing hide-and-seek.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:45.370
What?

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.930
After Godai came home
from Mitsutomo Corporation,

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.560
he locked himself up
in his room.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:55.020
Hmm...Maybe he made a fatal
mistake during the interview.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.110
I'm not sure.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.710
When I asked how it went

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.310
all he said was
"It was an easy delivery."

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.340
Ohh!

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:06.020
Why are you impressed?

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.540
It's a thoughtful answer
for someone like Godai.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.460
That must mean the interview
went well.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.970
You think?

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.840
But he sure is gloomy
considering it went well.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.200
Godai!

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:22.780
Oh!

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.150
Godai!
It's Yagami! Godai!

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.010
- You're wasting your time.
- Huh?

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.440
Godai is in hiding.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:36.690
Please explain why you
didn't show for the interview!

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:37.550
What?

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:43.970
Godai, is that true?
Open up!

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:46.760
Please, Godai!
Open up!

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.430
Godai! Godai!

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.430
Oh, what a nuisance!
I can't even sulk in peace.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.290
Godai!

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.150
Godai!

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.380
Godai!

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.860
It's awful quiet in there.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.590
Y-You're right.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.900
What if he committed suicide?!

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.180
As if!

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:15.320
Miss Yagami, don't say
things like that.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.880
We have no choice but to
ram down the door!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:19.690
Good idea!

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.110
Ready, and... !

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.470
W-Wait!

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:27.680
See? He came out.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.470
He's such a simpleton.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.310
- Godai!
- Godai!

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:34.000
I'm alive!
So leave me alone!

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.990
I'm sure... it's my fault.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:41.790
What?

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:48.490
Godai didn't want my father
to think he was using me.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:53.170
Really? But he had his hopes up
for the interview.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.100
But... there's no other reason.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:03.550
I'm sorry! To think he's suffering
because of me!

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.570
H-Hold on! That's just
what you think.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.200
I'm sure that's it!

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.110
Calm down, Miss Yagami.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:16.820
Look what Godai did, making
a young girl cry like that.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.290
- Hey.
- Yes?

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.240
How can you be calmly
watching TV like that?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.040
Shouldn't I be?

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.850
Aren't you worried
about your daughter?

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:34.240
Don't worry. I'm sure
she won't go off and elope.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:37.310
Elope?
Not with a guy like him!

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:41.650
But maybe she's being
deceived and...

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.240
Oh. Are you going out?

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.550
I'm going to Godai's.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:55.290
Stop crying.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.530
Godai just wasn't meant to
work at Mitsutomo Corporation.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:00.980
No, it's my father's fault.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:05.350
If only he had remembered who
Godai was when they first met.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.500
Dad!

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:16.950
Ibuki!

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:19.790
Go home, Dad!
Why'd you come here?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.820
- Come home right now, Ibuki!
- Huh?

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.250
We are going home
this minute!

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.230
No way! I'm never
going back to that house!

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.430
Want to throw this?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.220
Thank you.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:32.740
Let me go!

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.430
Yagami! Calm down!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.560
Hey, Godai! Just what
are you thinking?

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:41.570
You are despicable!

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:44.880
You deceived my daughter and
didn't show for your interview!

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:49.810
And now you've kidnapped Ibuki!
What are you going to make her do?

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.310
Kidnapped?

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:55.680
- What's he talking about?
- Should we throw this hammer?

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.320
N-No!

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:04.600
Please come in.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:11.130
Why did you ditch the interview?
I'll at least hear you out.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.650
Ditch?

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.040
Godai is not one to ditch.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:21.110
Shut up! You're being deceived.
What do you see in this clod, anyway?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:25.380
Just a minute! You're being
very one-sided here.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:28.650
Manager...

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.450
How can you call him a clod?
You don't even know him.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:37.900
Once you get to know him,
you'll see he's even more of a clod.

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:41.330
Be quiet! What are you
muttering over there?

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.300
Manager, you shouldn't be
so forceful.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.000
You're the one that's
being put down.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:48.750
Stand up for yourself!

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:49.600
Excuse me...

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:54.290
I'm sorry to interrupt.
Is there a Godai here?

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.940
I am he.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.850
H-Hello.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:04.430
I heard at the hospital that
you looked after my wife.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:08.050
Er...may I ask who you are?

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:13.170
My wife started having
contractions on the street.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:17.270
Godai was passing by
and called an ambulance.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:22.380
He even went with her
to the hospital. Thank you.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.940
The doctor said that my wife and
baby would've been in danger

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:28.700
had it been a minute later.
You are a lifesaver.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:30.290
N-Not at all.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:35.800
Godai, if that's the case
why didn't you admit it earlier?

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:40.660
W-Well, I didn't think it was a
good enough reason.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:48.470
- Godai, I had you wrong.
- Huh?

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:51.600
If you had ignored his wife and
rushed to your interview instead,

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.510
I would've felt scorn for you.

00:09:55.290 --> 00:10:00.800
It's true. This man stayed by
my wife's side in the ambulance,

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:02.680
and even bought her an
easy birth amulet.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.340
I see.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.320
Dad, now do you understand?

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.170
That's the kind of man
Godai is.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.450
Yes, he is a very remarkable
young man.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:21.820
If only we could have the likes
of him at our company.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:25.830
Dad! Are you saying...?!

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.970
It's regrettable.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:41.430
Very regrettable.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:47.560
Wait, Dad. What do you mean?

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:52.220
Today was my last chance to get
interviews for my recommendations.

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:56.010
No way! You were just saying
what a good man Godai was!

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.100
That has nothing to do with it.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.510
Hey, Ibuki! Wait!

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.410
Yagami!
Whaddaya think you're doing?

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:08.510
Miss Yagami!

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:14.590
That must be a cake to celebrate
the baby's birth! Am I right?

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:18.390
Ibuki!

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:23.820
Dad, until you do something about
Godai's employment,

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.430
I'm not going home.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.530
Ibuki! Come out this instant!

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:28.730
Miss Yagami!

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.140
Hey, this is my room!

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:33.800
I think this will drag on
for a while.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.880
It should be fun to watch.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.180
Things will get exciting
around here.

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:40.470
- Ibuki!
- Miss Yagami!

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.260
What are you thinking, Yagami?

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:00.590
Good morning!

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:04.030
Why, you're up early again.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:07.330
You're sure hanging in there.
Isn't this your third day already?

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.950
Yes, thank you.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:13.240
It's going to be another
interesting day.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:16.210
Yeah. I'm sure glad
to be alive.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:24.550
Godai, please get up.
It's morning.

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:30.090
It's such a nice day today.
Get up.

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:37.690
Huh? T-That's my sweatshirt!

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:43.000
I'm sorry. I had to borrow it since
I didn't bring any clothes with me.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:46.790
Come upstairs to eat.
I can't clean up until you're done.

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:04.320
Dear, I'll go today to try and
convince Ibuki to come home.

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:07.690
Let that twerp be.
She's no longer my daughter.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:12.190
How can you say that?
She's being an imposition too.

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:16.640
Regardless of the reason,
Godai missed his interview.

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:20.310
So why is he my responsibility now?

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:22.380
That may be true...

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:27.150
But Ibuki is stubborn
just like you.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.290
What do you mean?

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:31.820
Well, if we leave things
the way they are now,

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.490
Ibuki and Godai
might just...

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:37.890
I'll not have it!
Not with him, of all people!

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.000
Why, he seems like a nice
young man.

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:43.240
How can you say that?

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:46.000
Anyway, just let me
handle it.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:55.480
Hey, is it true that
you're staying at Godai's?

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.840
Yeah. I had a huge fight
with my dad.

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:02.120
Are you sure it's okay?
You still have school

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.630
and the homeroom teacher
will have a fit if she finds out.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:07.680
That's the least of
Yagami's concerns.

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.360
She's at the brink of
realizing her love.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:16.460
Yes, if I'm going to be
persecuted for this, then fine.

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:18.960
I'm living for love.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.700
That's awesome, Yagami.

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:22.610
Thanks.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:27.150
And so, this is hard
for me to ask but...

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:32.250
For now, my living expenses...
well...er...

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:36.280
in short...
can you guys cover me?

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.020
- Cover me.
- Okay.

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:54.430
Miss Yagami!

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.560
Are you grocery
shopping too, Miss Kyoko?

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:02.940
Weren't you barricading
yourself in room 5?

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:05.510
Yes, well, I had some
errands to run.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.490
- By the way, Miss Kyoko...
- Y-Yes?

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:11.340
Is there a lingerie store nearby?

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:16.550
Coffee House Chapa-Tei

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.630
Will Godai wear these?

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.900
It's a matching pair
with mine.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:29.570
Miss Yagami! Are you planning
to move in to Maison Ikkoku?

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:31.910
Yes.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.150
You are?

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:38.840
Why don't you go home?

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:43.290
No matter how hard you try,
you're not helping Godai's situation.

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:46.760
You're right.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.680
"You're right"?
Does that mean...?

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:53.050
- I was stupid.
- Huh?

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:59.160
My father can't recommend someone
who failed to show for his interview.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:04.240
D-Does that mean
you'll move back and...

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:07.610
I think I'll quit school.

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:10.750
Why?

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:15.670
Because if Godai can't find a job,
how will he pay his living expenses?

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:20.050
That's why I'll find a job
and support him.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.020
Isn't that a great idea?

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:32.320
Well, putting all
fantasy notions aside...

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.830
What? But I'm serious!

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:52.580
Kyoko, please don't tell
Godai what we talked about.

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:55.920
- I don't want to shock him.
- Of course I won't.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:59.590
If he heard your intentions,
he'll flip out and die on the spot.

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.930
- Huh?
- Oh!

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:05.930
Ibuki!

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.360
Mom!

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:14.400
Wait!
Ibuki, let's talk.

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:17.210
Talk?

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.720
Just come here.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:22.020
Trust me.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:37.620
Godai, here.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.360
- H-Hey!
- Ibuki!

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:57.840
Hey! Come on out!
Your mom's crying.

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:01.350
No! I know she's on
Dad's side.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.930
Ibuki, I'm on your side.

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:08.090
- Liar!
- Why would I lie?

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:11.440
After talking thing,s over
with Godai

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:13.740
I think he's a fine
young man.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:17.970
Really?
Do you really think that?

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:20.250
Sure, I do.

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:25.180
But I don't think it's a good idea
for you two to get together right now,

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:27.250
since you're still in school.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.570
I'm quitting school.

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:33.020
No, you have to graduate
from high school.

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:34.610
You understand that, right?

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:38.380
- What are they talking about?
- I don't know.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:43.560
Come out. Once you graduate,
I'll start the marriage talks.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:45.090
- What?
- H-Hey!

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:47.630
What are you saying?

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:52.670
Shh! Don't worry.
If I get her to come home for now,

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:55.980
things will have cooled down
by the time she graduates.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:59.840
Thank you, Mom,
for acknowledging our love.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:04.610
Let's go home then.
I'll make Dad understand.

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:11.550
What's wrong?
Come on out.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:15.330
No, Mom. I can't go home.

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:22.470
After all, I'm sure Dad will
make it so that

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:25.210
Godai and I can't
see each other anymore.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:34.340
I'm so sorry.

00:19:34.430 --> 00:19:36.880
I'll rethink my strategy
and come again.

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.310
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:44.990
- This is exhausting.
- Yes.

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:48.730
- Shall we have some tea?
- Good idea.

00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.060
Oh!

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.610
What? You couldn't
convince her?

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:12.790
And you call yourself
a mother?

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.450
What? She's seriously
in love with him?

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:18.530
I don't want to hear it.

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:23.350
I just don't get it.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.630
What does she see
in a guy like him?

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:41.860
How long am I going to have
to live in Room 3?

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:47.690
- Hi, Godai.
- M-Mr. Yagami!

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.650
Sorry to bother you,
but can you come with me?

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:55.470
I just want to get to
know you better.

00:20:55.830 --> 00:21:00.170
What? Is he saying
he'll get me into Mitsutomo?

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.170
Let me change first.

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:06.570
No need. I'm just bringing
you home with me.

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:34.040
Godai...

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:39.130
That's odd.

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:53.920
I hope he's not in
Kyoko's room again.

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:08.500
Err...

00:22:08.710 --> 00:22:09.930
Y-Yes?

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:12.750
- Godai...
- Huh?

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:13.820
W-Well...

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:18.870
- He's not home yet?
- No.

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:22.690
He sure is late, isn't he?
Where could he have gone?

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:24.310
Y-Yeah.

00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:27.540
So he's not in Kyoko's room either.

00:22:28.560 --> 00:22:32.730
You want to know what I plan to do with
my life once I enter the workforce?

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:37.230
Yes, it's important
so I need to know.

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:40.830
Sure. I don't have
unrealistic goals,

00:22:41.250 --> 00:22:45.140
but I hope to live a fulfilling life
that is suitable to me.

00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:50.250
I see.
That is a noble attitude.

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:59.140
By the way, Ibuki's blood type
is AB. What's yours?

00:22:59.390 --> 00:23:01.580
My blood type?

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:06.490
I'm A.

00:23:06.830 --> 00:23:10.460
No! A's and AB's don't
get along in love.

00:23:10.540 --> 00:23:13.530
- You can't have Ibuki!
- Huh?

00:23:15.840 --> 00:23:20.750
W-Wait a minute! Just what are
you questioning me for anyway?

00:23:34.230 --> 00:23:38.310
I think I'll make a great wife!
Yeah!

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:48.450
What?! Godai got a job?

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:51.830
- Congratulations, Godai.
- Let's party!

00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:53.870
Just a minute.

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:58.450
Next:
"All (Not So) Quiet on the Job-Hunt Front!
Godai's Eleventh-Hour Save"

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:02.160
I cannot speak of what's to come!
